    "title" "Survivor PDA Orchestrator"
    "description" "[h1]Survivor PDA Orchestrator[/h1] An adaptive event director for Project Zomboid and Survivor PDA (ProjectRPGExpanded). Runs in single player and multiplayer. The director is disabled by default.

[h2]Using PDA Admin[/h2] First enable the ProjectRPGExpanded Admin Panel in the game's Sandbox Options. Then open PDA Admin with Shift + F7 (the default key binding) and enable Orchestrator inside the panel. These are separate settings: enabling Admin Panel makes PDA Admin available; enabling Orchestrator starts the director.

[h2]Features[/h2] [list][*]Schedules opportunities, threats and rest, using native XP, Mystery Box Hunt, money, material and horde events.[*]Adaptive pacing remembers survivor tension, shares protection across nearby groups, and learns cautiously from observed horde outcomes. Night Events with sprinters lower director threat chance; quiet time gradually restores it.[*]Opportunity weights respond to group progression and combat, with a configurable rolling limit on bonuses.[*]Uses native ProjectRPG rewards, synchronization and event durations. It does not replace or end events started by admins or tickets.[*]Night Events are independently configurable, disabled by default, and can overlap other events. The default chance is 50% per night; four weighted levels tune container loot chance and sprinter presence.[*]Admins can start or end a Night Event in PDA Admin. Manual starts require Night Events to be enabled and it to be nighttime.[*]PDA Admin includes settings, diagnostics, a read-only decision simulation and a control to request an immediate director decision.[*]English and Brazilian Portuguese follow the PDA language. Extraction Mode support is optional.[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2] Project Zomboid Build 42.21+, ProjectRPGExpanded and ZombieBuddy 2.3.4+. Extraction Mode is optional.

Workshop ID: 3833288237
Mod ID: SurvivorPDAOrchestrator"
    "changenote" "Adds adaptive group tension, cautious horde outcome learning, Night Event threat pressure, contextual opportunity weights, a configurable bonus limit, and read-only decision simulation. Includes English and Brazilian Portuguese settings and diagnostics."
}
